###############################################
# NOTES FOR TESTING
###############################################

# HOW TO USE THIS FILE:
# 1. Install "REST Client" extension in VS Code
# 2. Start your backend server (npm run dev)
# 3. Run "Register Student" request first
# 4. Copy the token from response
# 5. Paste token in @studentToken variable at top
# 6. Repeat for merchant and admin tokens
# 7. Run other requests

# TESTING WORKFLOW:
# Phase 1: Authentication
#   - Register all user types
#   - Test login for each role
#   - Verify token authentication

# Phase 2: Basic Operations
#   - Get profiles and balances
#   - View transaction histories
#   - Test role-based access

# Phase 3: Payment Flow
#   - Student generates QR
#   - Copy entire qrData object from response
#   - Merchant processes with that qrData
#   - Verify balances updated
#   - Check transaction created

# Phase 4: Admin Operations
#   - Manage users
#   - Top-up balances
#   - View analytics

# Phase 5: Security Tests
#   - Test replay attacks (reuse nonce)
#   - Test expired QR (old timestamp)
#   - Test forged signatures
#   - Test role violations

# Phase 6: Error Handling
#   - Invalid inputs
#   - Unauthorized access
#   - Edge cases

# COMMON ERRORS & SOLUTIONS:
# - "Not authorized, no token" → Add token to Authorization header
# - "Invalid credentials" → Check email/password/role
# - "QR code expired" → Generate new QR (timestamp too old)
# - "QR code already used" → Generate new QR (nonce reused)
# - "Insufficient balance" → Use admin to top-up student
# - "Student/Merchant not found" → Check the ID is correct
